        <p class="craft3d__tags">Ahir · Suf · Paako</p>
        <p class="craft3d__copy">Each village of Kutch stitches its own signature: Suf counted from the reverse, Paako worked tight from the front, Aabhla caging a mirror in thread.</p>
        <a class="craft3d__link" href="/pages/video">Explore Crafts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="craft3d__panel">
        <p class="craft3d__no"><b>02</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="craft3d__name">Block print</h3>
        <p class="craft3d__tags">Hand block · Carved wood · Cotton</p>
        <p class="craft3d__copy">Cloth printed by hand with carved wooden blocks, the pattern laid down one press at a time along its length.</p>
        <a class="craft3d__link" href="/pages/video">Explore Crafts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="craft3d__panel">
        <p class="craft3d__no"><b>03</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="craft3d__name">Discharge print</h3>
        <p class="craft3d__tags">Dyed cloth · Discharge paste · By hand</p>
        <p class="craft3d__copy">The cloth is dyed first; a paste laid on by hand lifts the colour away, and the pattern shows where it was, a lighter shade of the cloth.</p>
        <a class="craft3d__link" href="/pages/video">Explore Crafts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      <article class="craft3d__panel">
        <p class="craft3d__no"><b>04</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="craft3d__name">Weaving</h3>
        <p class="craft3d__tags">Handloom · Extra weft · Kutch</p>
        <p class="craft3d__copy">Woven on the handlooms of Kutch, its motifs picked into the cloth with an extra weft, as its weavers have done for generations.</p>
        <a class="craft3d__link" href="/pages/video">Explore Crafts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
